{
  "module": "Attention: how tokens exchange information",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "attention-gist",
    "title": "Attention, at the highest level",
    "summary": "Why a token's starting vector is not enough, and the idea of attention: each position updates its vector with a weighted mix of information from the other positions.",
    "covers": ["attention-gist"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "embeddings",
        "reason": "Attention updates the token vectors the embedding step produces."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "sequence-shapes",
        "reason": "Attention looks across the n positions of the sequence."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "context-blind",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "After the embedding lookup, every token has a vector. But each vector was picked from the table "
            },
            {
              "text": "on its own",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", without looking at the tokens around it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So the word "
            },
            {
              "text": "bank",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " gets exactly the same starting vector in "
            },
            {
              "text": "the river bank",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and in "
            },
            {
              "text": "the bank account",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Its vector cannot yet reflect what the sentence is about."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 6, 17)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "the-idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Attention",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the mechanism that fixes this. It lets each token's vector be "
            },
            {
              "text": "updated using information from other tokens",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " in the sequence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Afterwards the vector for "
            },
            {
              "text": "bank",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " can carry something about "
            },
            {
              "text": "river",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " or about "
            },
            {
              "text": "account",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", depending on which neighbours it took information from."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 17)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "weighted-mix",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "How does a position decide what to take? For each position, the model works out "
            },
            {
              "text": "how relevant every other position is",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and then takes a "
            },
            {
              "text": "weighted mix",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " of their information."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A position that is very relevant gets a large weight and contributes a lot. One that is not relevant gets a small weight and contributes little."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 17)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "only-exchange",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Attention is the place where "
            },
            {
              "text": "different positions exchange information",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". The embedding lookup treats each token separately, and so does the tokenizer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The rest of the details of how the relevance is computed come in the next lessons. For now, hold on to the picture: "
            },
            {
              "text": "each position updates itself from a weighted mix of the others",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The word \"attention\" describes what the mechanism does. It is a piece of arithmetic on vectors. Nothing in it is paying attention in a human sense."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 17)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What does attention do, at the highest level?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It lets each token's vector be updated using information from other tokens in the sequence"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The update is a weighted mix of the other positions' information."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It splits the text into tokens"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the tokenizer's job, and it happens before the network."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It chooses which token comes next"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Choosing a token is sampling, after the network has finished."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It measures how wrong the model is"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the loss."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["the-idea", "weighted-mix"],
      "covers": ["attention-gist"],
      "variants": [
        {
